w: 1.~Je- sus, in Thy dy- ing woes, E- ven while Thy life- blood flows, 
w: 2.~Sa- vior, for our par- don sue, When our sins Thy pangs re- new, 
w: 3.~O may we, who mer- cy need, Be like Thee in heart and deed, 
w: 4.~Je- sus, pi- ty- ing the sighs Of the thief, who near Thee dies,
w: 5.~May we, in our guilt and shame, Still Thy love and mer- cy claim,
w: 6.~O re- mem- ber us who pine, Look- ing from our cross to Thine;
w: 7.~Je- sus, lov- ing to the end Her whose heart Thy sor- rows rend,
w: 8.~May we in Thy sor- rows share, And for Thee all per- il dare,
w: 9.~May we all Thy loved ones be, All one ho- ly fa- mi- ly,
w: 10.~Je- sus, whelmed in fears un- known, With our e- vil left a- lone,
w: 11.~When we vain- ly seem to pray, and our hope seems far a- way,
w: 12.~Though no Fa- ther seem to hear, Though no light our spir- its cheer,
w: 13.~Je- sus, in Thy thirst and pain, While Thy wounds Thy life- blood drain,
w: 14.~Thirst for us in mer- cy still; All Thy ho- ly work ful- fill;
w: 15.~May we thirst Thy love to know; Lead us in our sin and woe
w: 16.~Je- sus, all our ran- som paid, All Thy Fa- ther's will o- beyed,
w: 17.~Save us in our soul's dis- tress, Be our help to cheer and bless,
w: 18.~Brigh- ten all our hea- venward way, With an ev- er ho- lier ray,
w: 19.~Je- sus, all Thy la- bor vast, All Thy woe and con- flict past,
w: 20.~When the death shades round us lower, Guard us from the tem- per's power,
w: 21.~May Thy life and death sup- ply Grace to live and grace to die,
